## Project Summary

*AI-generated project summary produced by `/write-summary`, for future AI sessions catching up without re-analyzing line-by-line; may be out of date — re-run to refresh.*

### Purpose

Docker-based launcher for pre-made Claude Code agents. Each persona ships its own `CLAUDE.md` + optional `.conf` (model/params); all share OAuth credentials, workspace mapping, slash commands, skills, and toolchain caches. Instances are persistent named sessions per agent; prior conversations resume automatically. Filename *tags* and per-instance *modes* compose into a layered Docker image and per-launch behavior.

### Tech Stack

- Python 3.10+ host launcher (frozen dataclasses, walrus, modern unions); `prompt_toolkit` (picker TUI), `python-dotenv` (`.conf` parsing), `rich` (markdown previews); stdlib elsewhere (incl. `urllib` for CDN-range fetches, `readline` for tab-completion). No dependency manifest yet — deps live in `install_dependencies.sh`.
- Docker + Compose v2. Base image = debian:bookworm-slim + Claude Code + jq/yq/fd/tree/ripgrep; `[code]` adds Rust/Node/uv, `{auto}` adds iptables/sudo + firewall, `{DooD}` mounts the docker socket, `{web}` adds playwright.
- `unittest` suite (570 tests, <1s: `python3 -m unittest discover -s launch/tests`); `mypy launch/ run.py` + `ruff check .` both clean. No CI gate.

